  "defect_finding": {
    "title": "RTD-backed TOOL_OBSERVATION VMem admission never attaches metadata.toolCallId/artifactRef, so it can never become a proactive-paging candidate",
    "real_evidence": {
      "vmem_object": "obj-737affd6d8a2 (TOOL_OBSERVATION, title=rtd_artifact)",
      "metadata_json_observed": "{}",
      "code_location": "brainstem/prime-extension/src/index.ts, the `vmemAdmit(session, \"TOOL_OBSERVATION\", \"rtd_artifact\", {...})` call site (RTD admission ref #2) -- confirmed by reading the code directly: it is called with only 4 arguments (session, kind, title, content); the 5th `metadata` parameter vmemAdmit itself supports (and which the AutoInject admission call site DOES pass, e.g. packetMetadata) is never provided here, so [vmem_admission]'s `--metadata` CLI flag is never set for RTD admissions and the stored object's metadata_json is always `{}`."
    },
    "consequence": "context-paging.ts's byToolCallId correlation map ONLY reads `obj.metadata.toolCallId ?? obj.metadata.tool_call_id` (no fallback to the object's `content` JSON, unlike vmem.py's resolve_object which DOES fall back to parsing stored content for delivery_id/artifact_ref). An RTD-backed TOOL_OBSERVATION object therefore structurally can never correlate to a live toolResult message and can never be proactively paged, even though its content DOES contain a real, valid artifact_ref and fault-in via `vmem resolve` would still work fine for it (that path has the content-fallback). This exactly explains why this pilot's real context_paging event only ever claimed the AutoInject object (1 of 1 eligible candidates), never the RTD object, which remained RESIDENT (never evaluated as a paging candidate at all) for the whole session.",
    "status": "Discovered by the parent during independent evidence inspection. NOT fixed this pass, per Pilot 4's evidence-only discipline -- collected and reported, not repaired in the same pass."
  },
